PoolPilot for Debian/Ubuntu
===========================

Build:
  ./packaging/linux/build-deb.sh --version 0.1.0
  # 产物: packaging/out/poolpilot_<version>_amd64.deb

Install:
  sudo apt install ./packaging/out/poolpilot_0.1.0_amd64.deb

The service runs as the system user "poolpilot" and stores data in
/var/lib/poolpilot. The default HTTP endpoint is 0.0.0.0:5274.

Security warning
----------------
This package does not terminate TLS. The application session cookie is currently
issued without the Secure flag. Do not expose port 5274 directly to the public
Internet. Use a firewall/VPN, or change ASPNETCORE_URLS to 127.0.0.1:5274 and put
nginx/caddy in front for TLS.

Configuration:
  /etc/default/poolpilot
  sudo systemctl restart poolpilot

Public pages are enabled by default in this package:
  PublicPages__Leads=true
  PublicPages__Followers=true
  Set either to false to return its endpoints to 404.

Disable login/registration (public-only deployment):
  Auth__AccountsEnabled=false
  This makes /api/auth login/register/MFA and /api/setup return 404. The public
  header hides the login/register links automatically. Existing session cookies
  are not revoked by this switch.

Logs:
  journalctl -u poolpilot -f

Health:
  curl http://127.0.0.1:5274/api/health
